            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It might make sense indeed. There was a similar suggestion for 'mini.ai' (#1802) and the [initial reasoning applies to 'mini.surround'](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1802#issuecomment-2886729738). But as `MiniAi.move_cursor()` adds to jumplist, it might be a good idea to also make `MiniSurround.find()` do the same. I'll take a look.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It might make sense indeed. There was a similar suggestion for 'mini.ai' (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3068942782\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1802\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1802/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1802\">#1802</a>) and the <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1802#issuecomment-2886729738\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1802/hovercard\">initial reasoning applies to 'mini.surround'</a>. But as <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniAi.move_cursor()</code> adds to jumplist, it might be a good idea to also make <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniSurround.find()</code> do the same. I'll take a look.</p>",
            "bodyText": "It might make sense indeed. There was a similar suggestion for 'mini.ai' (#1802) and the initial reasoning applies to 'mini.surround'. But as MiniAi.move_cursor() adds to jumplist, it might be a good idea to also make MiniSurround.find() do the same. I'll take a look.",
